							</xmi:Extension>
							<ownedComment xmi:type='uml:Comment' xmi:id='_17_0_2_4_854026d_1383055395603_142023_2716' body='&lt;html&gt;&#10;  &lt;head&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;style&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;p {padding:0px; margin:0px;}&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/style&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/head&gt;&#10;  &lt;body&gt;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;The diagram displays the &lt;i&gt;PartOrUsageRelatedSpecifications&lt;/i&gt; for Cavity seals and plugs. Both are used to seal &lt;i&gt;Cavities&lt;/i&gt;. A cavity plug is used for a single cavity that has no wire in it, a cavity seal is used to seal a single cavity together with a terminal and a wire.&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;For both are special types existent that do not seal a single cavity, but a couple of cavities at the same time. The &lt;i&gt;MultiCavitySeal&lt;/i&gt; and the &lt;i&gt;MultiCavityPlug&lt;/i&gt;. For more details see the description of the corresponding classes.&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;  &lt;/body&gt;&#10;&lt;/html&gt;&#10;'>
								<annotatedElement xmi:idref='EAID_F2B4EF74_C4BE_4498_B806_5FFD8D63A817'/>
							</ownedComment>
						</ownedDiagram>
						<ownedDiagram xmi:type='uml:Diagram' xmi:id='_17_0_2_4_854026d_1383059683423_926988_2729' name='Wire Protections' visibility='public' ownerOfDiagram='_17_0_2_4_854026d_1382969329975_216295_3207'>
