							<ownedComment xmi:type='uml:Comment' xmi:id='_17_0_2_4_854026d_1383731809289_502826_3043' body='&lt;html&gt;&#10;  &lt;head&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;style&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;p {padding:0px; margin:0px;}&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/style&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/head&gt;&#10;  &lt;body&gt;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;A &lt;i&gt;CompatibilitySpecification&lt;/i&gt; is a container for various &lt;i&gt;CompatibilityStatements&lt;/i&gt;. Each &lt;i&gt;CompatibilityStatement&lt;/i&gt; can reference dedicated elements in order to state compatibility (in case of the attribute &lt;i&gt;hasCompatibility&lt;/i&gt; is true) respectively in order to state non-compatibility (in case of the attribute &lt;i&gt;hasCompatibility &lt;/i&gt;is false).&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;To express the compatibility between &lt;i&gt;PartVersions&lt;/i&gt; the &lt;i&gt;CompatibilityStatement &lt;/i&gt;references the &lt;i&gt;PartOrUsageRelatedSpecifications &lt;/i&gt;(or sub elements of them) those describe the technical properties of the relevant &lt;i&gt;PartVersions&lt;/i&gt;.&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;  &lt;/body&gt;&#10;&lt;/html&gt;&#10;'>
								<annotatedElement xmi:idref='EAID_288953AD_1C88_44e8_AF03_5DC0658818F0'/>
							</ownedComment>
						</ownedDiagram>
