				<packagedElement xmi:type='uml:Enumeration' xmi:id='EAID_95EFB873_9AFB_4577_9F2A_D19BD7B1EA6A' name='PrimaryPartType'>
					<ownedComment xmi:type='uml:Comment' xmi:id='EAID_95EFB873_9AFB_4577_9F2A_D19BD7B1EA6ADocumentation' body='&lt;html&gt;&#10;  &lt;head&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;style&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;p {padding:0px; margin:0px;}&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/style&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/head&gt;&#10;  &lt;body&gt;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;The primary type of the part defines the type of the part (e.g. ConnectorHousing, Fixing, etc.) Since the VEC supports dual use parts (e.g. Fixing &amp;amp; WireProtection) the primary part type is necessary to define which specification associated to part is the primary character of the part. Therefore all primary part types correspond to a PartOrUsageRelatedSpecification (e.g. ConnectorHousing --&amp;gt; ConnectorHousingSpecification).&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;The primary part type &#39;Other&#39; is used if the PartVersion is not further specified by the VEC, which means it has no PartOrUsageRelatedSpecification, only a GeneralTechnicalPartSpecification or a direct instance of PartOrUsageRelatedSpecification.&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;  &lt;/body&gt;&#10;&lt;/html&gt;&#10;'>
						<annotatedElement xmi:idref='EAID_95EFB873_9AFB_4577_9F2A_D19BD7B1EA6A'/>
					</ownedComment>
